 "method": "DEPTH pass: additional pieces from furniture makers already present in furniture-na.json, furniture-mx.json and furniture-eu.json, researched via live web search against each brand's own product pages (domain-restricted WebSearch queries against ashleyfurniture.com, westelm.com, crateandbarrel.com, article.com, burrow.com, floydhome.com, joybird.com, la-z-boy.com, structube.com, eq3.com, dfs.co.uk, dunelm.com, loaf.com, harveynorman.ie, coppel.com, dico.com.mx, liverpool.com.mx). Direct page retrieval (WebFetch) was blocked with HTTP 403/404 on every one of these domains except burrow.com and article.com, where it succeeded and is marked below; every other product's price and dimensions were read from the search tool's quoted extraction of the live brand page text, not estimated. Only piece kinds already used in the three source files were used (sofa, armchair, diningChair, diningTable, bookcase, chestOfDrawers); no wardrobe or officeChair pieces met the honesty bar this pass, and 'bedFrame' was not introduced because none of the three source files use that kind. Where a brand page showed a current/sale price next to a labelled regular, original, 'was' or RRP price, the regular/original/RRP figure was recorded (Burrow, Joybird, Floyd's Gere chair and shelving, La-Z-Boy's Wilmette starting price, Harvey Norman Ireland's RRP, Coppel's 'antes' price, Structube's pre-sale regular price), matching the convention already used for these same perpetual-discount storefronts in furniture-na.json/furniture-eu.json. Ashley, West Elm, Crate & Barrel, Article, Dunelm, DFS, Loaf and Muebles Dico prices are each page's plain listed price with no separate higher figure found. Joybird's Jolie Accent Chair had only one price shown (no crossed-out original) and is recorded as such. A chair sold only as a two-chair SKU (West Elm Classic Café Dining Chair, Structube TROY Dining Armchair) is recorded with seats:1 per chair and the pair/SKU price, with 'set of 2' noted in type, matching the CB2/Target set convention in furniture-na.json. Pieces for which a search returned a price but no matching width+depth+height on the same brand page, or vice versa, were dropped rather than guessed: West Elm Austin Swivel Armchair, Pierce Low Bookcase, Wright 6-Drawer Dresser and Framework/Slope/Lenox dining chairs (fabric-dependent price ranges, no single figure); Pottery Barn was tried across armchairs, dining tables and bookcases and dropped entirely, as in furniture-na.json, because every candidate's price was either a multi-size/multi-fabric range or its page gave no width/depth; Ashley Woodanville Dining Chair, Caitbrook/Kristiland dining tables (set-only pricing) and Lobink office chair (no dimensions); Crate & Barrel Chelsea round tables (no height found) and Lafayette dresser (no dimensions); DFS Jose/Comida/Dip dining chairs and John Lewis ANYDAY Fern table (price or dimensions missing, or page shown as no longer available); Habitat 60 Scoop Fabric Chair (price inconsistent across three Argos pages, £275/£285/£384, with no way to tell which was current); Structube RENO/AFREEN/JERRY dining tables and RENO bookcase (incomplete or internally inconsistent dimension sets). Liverpool.com.mx and Coppel.com.mx searches that returned only marketplace sale prices with no visible regular price, or dimensions baked into an unreadable image, were likewise dropped; Coppel's Sofa Cama Oliver Gris and Muebles Dico's six pieces were the only two Mexican retailers that produced a clean regular-price-plus-dimensions pair this pass beyond what furniture-mx.json already had. Inches were converted to cm at x2.54 and rounded to 1 decimal; cm figures already stated in cm (Structube, Dunelm, DFS, Loaf, Harvey Norman, Coppel, Dico) were kept as read. taxIncluded follows the convention already set per market in the three source files (false for US/CA, true for GB/IE/MX). flatPack is left null throughout; no page read this pass used explicit flat-pack/assembly-required language strongly enough to confirm it either way for a given SKU.",
